{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And as for</b> [the phrase] די חסף די פחר — [it means] a clay vessel of the potter. And behold, he explained on account of this [the phrase] מלכו פליגא." "<b>נצבתא</b> — like [the Hebrew] כח [strength]." "<b>מערב</b> — like [the verse] 'and they mingled among the nations' (ובעברית: ויתערבו בגוים)."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrases are retained in Hebrew script as quoted; Ibn Ezra is glossing Daniel 2:41's Aramaic words."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:32.352872325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}